	(text "BEETLE C3 POWER TOPOLOGY / USB + OPTIONAL PROTECTED 1S"
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3463ae57-eef9-4216-b188-0c3da07dbc3f")
	)
	(text "R45: 0.82 ohm / 0.5 W at 70 C, derate above.\nReplaces Beetle 0.8 ohm: +8 mV drop at 400 mA."
		(at 106.68 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4b4793d5-f5de-49b2-953c-56f770df034b")
	)
	(text "RT9080: no boost; cell dropout and USB thermal derating apply. No generator AUX.\nCommon ground, no galvanic isolation or sustained HV-to-PC protection. NOT FOR ENERGIZATION.\nReference: DFR0868 V2.0 (2022-02-08); model evidence: components/beetle-power-v2/."
		(at 25.4 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "56b74424-79c0-436d-ba8c-d7c100bfa876")
	)
	(text "400 mA nominal charge study\nJP20 OPEN = charge disabled"
		(at 30.48 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9b2f0100-38e0-44b8-863b-b68f3c2efd37")
	)
	(text "Q20 AO3401A, D20 SS1H10 and D21 LED are independent prototype selections.\nR51 = 1k limits leakage-induced gate rise; adds 5 mA at 5 V. Verify hot switching and USB dropout.\nJP20 service interlock defaults OPEN. Close only for a qualified protected 4.2 V cell and source.\nNo cell NTC or active total USB-current limit. 400 mA charge does not fit every PC USB budget.\nLogic follows a usable source; unplug the cell for storage. No automatic wake/latch."
